The main reason most warlocks in classic WoW are seen with voidwalkers instead of succubi is due to the fact that voidwalkers provide more survivability and utility in group content, while succubi are generally better for solo play or PvP situations.

Here are some key points to consider:

1. Voidwalkers have a taunt ability called "Torment" which can be used to draw aggro from mobs, making them a valuable asset in group content. Succubi, on the other hand, do not have a taunt ability, making them less useful in group situations.

2. Voidwalkers have a passive ability called "Consume Shadows" which allows them to regenerate health out of combat. This can be helpful in long dungeon runs or when the warlock is not taking damage. Succubi do not have this ability, so they rely on the warlock's own health regeneration.

3. Voidwalkers have an ability called "Sacrifice" which allows them to absorb a portion of the damage taken by the warlock. This can be useful in high-damage situations or when the warlock is low on health. Succubi do not have this ability, so they cannot provide the same level of survivability.

4. Voidwalkers have an ability called "Suffering" which allows them to taunt multiple enemies at once, making them useful in situations where there are multiple mobs attacking the group. Succubi do not have this ability, so they are less useful in these situations.

5. Succubi have an ability called "Lash of Pain" which deals shadow damage to a single target. While this can be useful in PvP situations or when soloing, it is not as useful in group content as the taunt and survivability abilities provided by voidwalkers.

6. Succubi have an ability called "Seduction" which allows them to crowd control a single humanoid enemy, making them useful in PvP situations or when soloing. However, this ability is not as useful in group content as the taunt and survivability abilities provided by voidwalkers.

7. Succubi have an ability called "Lesser Invisibility" which allows them to become stealthed, making them useful in PvP situations or when soloing. However, this ability is not as useful in group content as the taunt and survivability abilities provided by voidwalkers.

8. Succubi have an ability called "Soothing Kiss" which reduces threat generated by the warlock, making them useful in PvP situations or when soloing. However, this ability is not as useful in group content as the taunt and survivability abilities provided by voidwalkers.

In summary, voidwalkers are generally considered better for group content due to their taunt and survivability abilities, while succubi are generally considered better for solo play or PvP situations due to their crowd control and stealth abilities.

It's worth noting that player preference and playstyle also play a big role in the choice of pet, and some players may prefer the look or playstyle of one pet over the other.
